@startuml
hide circle
skinparam nodesep 60
skinparam ranksep 70
skinparam padding 3

entity "users" as users {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  * email : text <<UQ>>
  * created_at : timestamptz
}

entity "sources" as sources {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  subject_user_id : uuid <<FK users, NULL>>
  * source_type : source_type_enum
  uri : text
  * created_at : timestamptz
}

entity "source_permissions" as perms {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  * source_id : uuid <<FK sources>>
  * user_id : uuid <<FK users>>
  * permission : permission_enum
  * granted_at : timestamptz
  --
  UQ (source_id, user_id)
}

entity "documents" as documents {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  * content_hash : bytea <<UQ>>
  * source_id : uuid <<FK sources>>
  * bronze_uri : text
  * created_at : timestamptz
  supersedes_id : uuid <<FK documents, NULL>>
  replaced_by_id : uuid <<FK documents, NULL>>
}

documents }o--|| sources
sources   }o--o| users : "subject"
sources   ||--o{ perms
perms     }o--|| users
documents |o--o| documents

note right of sources
  source_type: notion | gdrive | imap | web | file

  uri identifies which one:
  the scraped URL, Drive folder,
  mailbox or file path.

  subject_user_id = whose information
  this is. NULL for an unattended
  web scrape.
end note

note bottom of perms
  permission: control | read

  control = full CRUD on the source.
  read    = may retrieve its documents.

  user_id = who has access.
  permission = what type of access.

  UQ (source_id, user_id) allows only one
  grant per user per source.
end note

note left of documents
  id is derived, not random:
  uuidv5(APP_NAMESPACE, content_hash),
  where APP_NAMESPACE is a fixed
  constant in code. Same content always
  yields the same id, so re-ingesting
  a file is a no-op.

  Revision chain, both directions:
  supersedes_id  -> the older row this
    one replaced. NULL = first version.
  replaced_by_id -> the newer row that
    replaced this one. NULL = current.
end note
@enduml
